1588','off'),(1093,'_site_transient_theme_roots','a:5:{s:18:\"beanchilling-theme\";s:7:\"/themes\";s:15:\"hello-elementor\";s:7:\"/themes\";s:16:\"twentytwentyfive\";s:7:\"/themes\";s:16:\"twentytwentyfour\";s:7:\"/themes\";s:17:\"twentytwentythree\";s:7:\"/themes\";}','off'),(1068,'_transient_timeout_bc_chatbot_prompt','1778501353','off'),(1069,'_transient_bc_chatbot_prompt','You are BeanBot, the helpful assistant for the BeanChilling project website. BeanChilling is a GIS-based coffee farm mapping and profiling application developed by Team Zenith. The platform helps coffee producers map their farms and profile their coffees to make better field-level decisions. Answer questions about the project concisely and helpfully based on the context below. If asked about topics unrelated to BeanChilling or coffee farming, politely redirect the user. Keep answers under 4 sentences unless more detail is specifically requested.\n\nProject content from the website:\n\n\n[Team Zenith]\nWho We Are Zenith Research and Development Team Zenith is the multidisciplinary team building BeanChilling. We combine geographic analysis, agricultural insights, and modern development practices to create useful field tools for coffee farmers. Researchers and Developers Place your final names, roles, and mugshots here when ready. Photo Researcher / Developer 01 Role placeholder: GIS Analyst Photo Researcher / Developer 02 Role placeholder: Data Specialist Photo Researcher / Developer 03 Role placeholder: Frontend Engineer Photo Researcher / Developer 04 Role placeholder: Backend Engineer\n\n[IMRAD]\nResearch Details BeanChilling Research Through IMRAD This page summarizes the research framework and can be expanded with your full manuscript details. Introduction Describe the context of coffee farming challenges, GIS opportunities, and why BeanChilling was proposed. Methods Explain data gathering, profiling workflow, mapping techniques, validation process, and development approach. Results Present key findings, app output examples, and indicators showing improved profiling and mapping quality. Discussion Interpret the findings, limitations, practical implications for farmers, and possible future enhancements.\n\n[App Showcase]\nApplication Walkthrough BeanChilling Feature Showcase This page is ready for your app screenshots and feature explanations. Replace placeholder blocks with final images later. Screenshot Placeholder Farm Mapping Module Show how farmers draw boundaries, geotag locations, and register farm plots. Screenshot Placeholder Coffee Profiling Module Show profile creation, quality descriptors, and farm-linked coffee records. Screenshot Placeholder Insight Dashboard Show summary metrics, map layers, and decision support features for users.\n\n[Home]\n[bc_section id=&#8221;107&#8243;][bc_section id=&#8221;108&#8243;][bc_section id=&#8221;109&#8243;][bc_section id=&#8221;110&#8243;]\n\n[GIS Coffee Profiling Platform]\nGIS Coffee Profiling Platform BeanChilling helps farmers map farms and profile coffees with clarity. BeanChilling is an improved GIS-based application currently in development. The platform combines farm mapping and coffee profiling so coffee producers can make better field-level decisions. Explore App FeaturesRead Research Summary','off'),(1098,'_site_transient_update_plugins','O:8:\"stdClass\":5:{s:12:\"last_checked\";i:1778500709;s:8:\"response\";a:0:{}s:12:\"translations\";a:0:{}s:9:\"no_update\";a:4:{s:51:\"all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall/wp-security.php\";O:8:\"stdClass\":10:{s:2:\"id\";s:49:\"w.org/plugins/all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall\";s:4:\"slug\";s:35:\"all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall\";s:6:\"plugin\";s:51:\"all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall/wp-security.php\";s:11:\"new_version\";s:5:\"5.4.7\";s:3:\"url\";s:66:\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall/\";s:7:\"package\";s:84:\"https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/all-in-one-wp-security-and-firewall.5.4.7.zip\";s:5:\"icons\";a:2:{